-- §6.2 T4 in a NON-ENTRY module: the multi-module twin of
-- `s6-2-t4-open-goal-deferred.mdk`, so the open-goal reject is graded where an
-- imported module's diagnostics travel (`run`/`build`'s multi-module arm).
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived, not captured). `libPick`'s goal is
-- `Sh (Q Int Bool (List a))`, `a` determined by nothing. Both ⊑-incomparable heads
-- match it and every binding of `a` keeps them matching, so the goal is ambiguous at
-- quiescence: `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` on every verb, located in lib.mdk at the goal
-- (R-SC3, #1183). Never a declaration-order commitment.
--
-- The declarations are ALSO an §6.1 condition (a) overlap, so `W-INCOMPARABLE-IMPLS`
-- is recorded beside the error; the section-5 rows name the reject by its own text.
import lib.{libPick}

main = println libPick
